      { kind: "p", lead: "Health information.", text: "Health information. Some countries treat health-related data, including inferences, under specific laws. If you live in Washington State, our separate Consumer Health Data Privacy Notice at dezbatere.ro/privacy/us-health-data applies. The end-of-debate check in section 4 can find that a debate's synthesis falls in the category “tendencies to suicide or harming other people”, and such a result can be an inference about your health. A debate with that result is deleted at once from the live service (section 6), and the result becomes unreadable with it there; section 7 says what trace remains and what our backups keep. Nobody reads the debate first, and no reviewer ever sees it. Once the debate finishes, you are not shown the debate's answer either: every finished debate is held until the check answers, while a running debate's page shows the arguments and the conclusion as they are composed. Only when the check cannot answer in time is the finished answer shown, and the debate is then checked again when you press Publish. Our question check (section 4) reads each question before a debate starts, and a question can reveal your health, for example when it reads like the words of a person in crisis. Its outcome decides only whether the debate starts or help numbers are shown, and nothing of it is kept. The support chat also recognises a message that reads like the words of a person in crisis, by a list of phrases or by the assistant's model, and then shows help numbers instead of an answer; we keep nothing of the message or of the reply, and the chat opens no case." }
